cff-version: 1.2.0
message: >-
  If you use Penicillium, please cite the software and the two IndPenSim papers it implements
  (Goldrick et al. 2015 and 2019, listed under references). Penicillium is MIT-licensed; the parts
  derived from IndPenSim are also under IndPenSim's BSD 3-Clause License (Copyright (c) 2016, Stephen Goldrick).
title: "Penicillium: a validated, pip-installable Python implementation of the IndPenSim penicillin fermentation simulator"
